    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to `POST /api/owners` (and mirrored it on `PUT /api/owners/{ownerId}`), keeping the flat `address` fully backward-compatible.\n\n**Contract (`openapi.yml`)**\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (so they're accepted on input and returned on `Owner`), and documented `address` as the composed return value.\n- Removed `address` from the required list \u2014 an owner is now valid with *either* a non-blank `addressLine1` or the flat `address`, plus `city`. `firstName`/`lastName`/`telephone` remain required. (The DTO is generated from this spec at build time.)\n\n**Persistence**\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields (columns `address_line1`/`address_line2`) to the `Owner` entity and dropped the now-invalid `@NotEmpty` on `address`.\n- Added the two columns to all four schema files (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 h2, mysql, postgres), and relaxed h2's `address NOT NULL`.\n\n**Behavior**\n- `OwnerAddress.compose(line1, line2, flat)`: normalizes each input (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET` etc.); when `addressLine1` is present returns the normalized line1 with a single space + normalized line2 appended when line2 is present; otherwise falls back to the normalized flat `address`.\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` (POST) and `ValidateOwner` (PUT) now normalize the structured fields, store them (null when blank), and set `address` to the composed value. The required-field check runs against that composed value, so it's blank only when *neither* form supplies an address.\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT) now copies `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` through as well.\n\nBecause the stored `address` now holds the structured-preferred composed value, everything that reads the owner's address uses the structured fields when present and falls back to the flat address.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest` (structured normalize/compose + flat-address backward-compat) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
